From: gvwifi-los23 build kit
Subject: [PATCH] sched: init cpufreq task stats before get_cpu() in sched_fork

cpufreq_task_stats_init() does kzalloc(GFP_KERNEL) but was called after
get_cpu() (preemption disabled): "BUG: sleeping function called from invalid
context" on every fork under CONFIG_DEBUG_ATOMIC_SLEEP, and a possible
scheduling-while-atomic hang under memory pressure. Call it first.

---
diff --git a/kernel/sched/core.c b/kernel/sched/core.c
index a263ba40..2553cbb7 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/core.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/core.c
@@ -1848,12 +1848,15 @@ void set_numabalancing_state(bool enabled)
 void sched_fork(struct task_struct *p)
 {
 	unsigned long flags;
-	int cpu = get_cpu();
+	int cpu;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_STAT
+	/* Allocates with GFP_KERNEL: must run before get_cpu(). */
 	cpufreq_task_stats_init(p);
 #endif
 
+	cpu = get_cpu();
+
 	__sched_fork(p);
 	/*
 	 * We mark the process as running here. This guarantees that
